      "article_id": "a1_eeeacb3839159d6f24ad6c6d",
      "headline": "Two variants of Nvidia's RTX Spark show up on Geekbench, revealing a cut-down 18-core model — Full 20-core beats most x86 mobile chips across multi-core and single-core tests",
      "confirmed_facts": [
        {
          "fact_id": "f1",
          "text": "Both parts score remarkably close to each other, posting impressive multi-core numbers, but their single-core performance isn't special.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-10T08:02:44.248458+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "3eb32dd20be9641d86b0f5d225e151b72b586646c1caede72073f5f730da971d",
          "excerpt": "Both parts score remarkably close to each other, posting impressive multi-core numbers, but their single-core performance isn't special.",
          "sentence_hash": "798b66954a39d21e675644a72b30fa6a91ff15ee496d2c921d396fc16a12206d",
          "anchors": [
            "but"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f2",
          "text": "Still, these are preliminary results on unreleased hardware, so take these numbers with a grain of salt.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-10T08:02:44.248489+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "3eb32dd20be9641d86b0f5d225e151b72b586646c1caede72073f5f730da971d",
          "excerpt": "Still, these are preliminary results on unreleased hardware, so take these numbers with a grain of salt.",
          "sentence_hash": "3d82df13764ab855e86264dd2b8b84e99e73b24d4f24295703e50532480c8156",
          "anchors": [
            "ai"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f3",
          "text": "It scored 2,541 points in the single-core test, so within 1% of the 20-core part, while the multi-core was 21,776 points, which is about 6% faster than the full-fat chip.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-10T08:02:44.248531+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "3eb32dd20be9641d86b0f5d225e151b72b586646c1caede72073f5f730da971d",
          "excerpt": "It scored 2,541 points in the single-core test, so within 1% of the 20-core part, while the multi-core was 21,776 points, which is about 6% faster than the full-fat chip.",
          "sentence_hash": "ff7bc9d2715334e4331707bedb5e370a488d1c14defb41c18a638f7ff66af14b",
          "anchors": [
            "1%",
            "6%",
            "full"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f4",
          "text": "The Snapdragon X2 Elite Extreme currently holds the record for the highest multi-core score with 25,075 points, so both SKUs of the RTX Spark lose to it.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-10T08:02:44.248560+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "3eb32dd20be9641d86b0f5d225e151b72b586646c1caede72073f5f730da971d",
          "excerpt": "The Snapdragon X2 Elite Extreme currently holds the record for the highest multi-core score with 25,075 points, so both SKUs of the RTX Spark lose to it.",
          "sentence_hash": "dbf3fbd57e081a8a281d966cc7c806a9ffcfcf3cac75169d40ceb909ad9c6db3",
          "anchors": [
            "both"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f5",
          "text": "But when we switch to the AMD AI Max+ 395, which scores 20,609 on average in the same test, even the 18-core Nvidia chip is 5.6% faster here, and the 20-core variant is about 12% faster.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-10T08:02:44.248586+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "3eb32dd20be9641d86b0f5d225e151b72b586646c1caede72073f5f730da971d",
          "excerpt": "But when we switch to the AMD AI Max+ 395, which scores 20,609 on average in the same test, even the 18-core Nvidia chip is 5.6% faster here, and the 20-core variant is about 12% faster.",
          "sentence_hash": "482b4713e94ab0259740377147e0722b7c1397f6c49faf5024563c577609ac6c",
          "anchors": [
            "12%",
            "5.6%",
            "6%"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact_id": "f6",
          "text": "Compared to Apple's lineup, the 20-core RTX Spark is 3.3% faster than the 14-core variant of the M3 Max, which scores 22,385 points in the multi-core bench.",
          "source_id": "source:primary",
          "captured_at": "2026-08-10T08:02:44.248609+08:00",
          "content_sha256": "3eb32dd20be9641d86b0f5d225e151b72b586646c1caede72073f5f730da971d",
          "excerpt": "Compared to Apple's lineup, the 20-core RTX Spark is 3.3% faster than the 14-core variant of the M3 Max, which scores 22,385 points in the multi-core bench.",
          "sentence_hash": "0841d062d234e4025c4f052af925f376510b7dbcb1195149b2dd0665bfa8b980",
          "anchors": [
            "3.3%"
          ]
        }
      ],
